CORE no-new-smt
exists_in_forall.c
--no-malloc-may-fail --pointer-check
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d* for all z, there exists a y so that y = z \+ 10 and y > 1: SUCCESS
\[main\.pointer_dereference\.\d+\] line \d+ dereference failure: pointer NULL in \*i: SUCCESS
\[main\.pointer_dereference\.\d+\] line \d+ dereference failure: deallocated dynamic object in \*i: SUCCESS
\[main\.pointer_dereference\.\d+\] line \d+ dereference failure: pointer outside dynamic object bounds in \*i: SUCCESS
--
--
The assertion reference number here is present so that we make sure
we always match the properties of the dereference inside the exists.
